message.content:
Read-only adversarial pre-review for PR #638 in /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto (branch origin/wp-interactive-cli-compare; diff with `git diff origin/main...origin/wp-interactive-cli-compare`). The interactive prompt code (crates/callisto-cli/src/tty.rs and the add wizard's prompt calls) is being rewritten on the inquire crate, so skip signal and terminal-state details in tty.rs. Known findings already being fixed (don't report): json-mode eligibility before --summary validation; preselection failure must warn and continue; pty test Session teardown; editor SIGINT (dismissed, git precedent).

Hunt in the rest of the change, which survives the rewrite, for what an automated reviewer would flag next:
- the add command's non-interactive path: --package/--summary/--bump flag combinations, unknown or duplicate packages, ambiguous names (foo vs cargo/foo), groups, private packages, empty workspace; error codes and messages vs docs/specs/cli.json and docs/errors.md;
- changed-package detection used for preselection (crates/callisto-graph/src/changed.rs and callers): correctness against tags, untagged packages, renamed or moved packages, paths with spaces, leading ':' or '-', newlines, and git process count (AGENTS.md: no git process per package);
- the review screen and written changeset: what is written vs what was shown (same structure?), file naming collisions, atomic_write use, changeset format round-trip;
- --format json output shape for add, stderr vs stdout, next-step line;
- the editor helper: environment filtering via the runner, temp file cleanup on every path, VISUAL/EDITOR with arguments and quoting;
- Rust: _ arms on our enums, unwrap/expect, swallowed errors, global state, visibility;
- tests that don't assert the behaviour they name.

For each issue: file:line, a concrete scenario, smallest fix. Verify against the code; drop speculation. Under 30 lines, most severe first; say plainly if nothing.

